From f59b936d043d08c0274a806762fed941bafb69c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:21:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ss-delta: Ad Hoc Play between copies of the game

- ss-delta.exe --player N (2-4): its own Vita user (saves copied from player 1's on its first
  start), config and log in ss-delta/player<N>/, ss-delta-player<N>.ini overrides; it reads the
  shader and pipeline caches without writing them (Config/renderer shader_cache_read_only)
- [multiplayer] network = local (default): copy N has the ad hoc address 127.0.0.N, P2P sockets
  bound to any address bind it, and a broadcast goes to every other copy (net_utils local ad hoc);
  lan is Vita3K's way, [multiplayer] adapter its adhoc-addr
- P2P datagram sockets ignore Windows' WSAECONNRESET after a datagram to a closed port
- [multiplayer] gamepad = n: only the nth gamepad (CtrlState::only_gamepad), also in the background
- SceNetInternal_689B9D7D (imported by adhoc_matching.suprx): a random number (hypothesis)
- the loader places a relocatable module with recompiled code where that code was generated for,
  when free (aot_preferred_base): the matching module loads only when Ad Hoc Play opens
- --dump-elfs also loads the matching module before quitting, so the installer gets its ELF

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
